Vendor-only register: NOT in the data sheet. The vendor driver (`ahci_sys.c`, `HI_SATA_PHY1_CTLH` = 0x64) sets bit 12 and writes 0x2521 as for SATA_PHY0_CTLH; the layout is assumed to be the same as SATA_PHY0_CTLH. Open question: on the Hi3520D board (under Linux, after the vendor sequence wrote this register) it read back 0, so the register may not exist on this chip (the Hi3520D has one SATA PHY) or is write-only. Not read at the stock U-Boot prompt: the SATA clocks are off there (PERI_CRG45 = 0), so the SATA host registers were not read.";

        enum SATA_PHY1_CTLH_use_refclk_alt_enum {
