        reg {
            name = "PHY control register";
            desc = "SATA_PORT_PHYCTL is a PHY control register.

Per-port value written by the init sequence. Data sheet 14.7.5.4 step 8: 0x0E262709 for 1.5 Gbit/s, 0x0E662709 for 3 Gbit/s (this is the vendor default `CONFIG_HI_SATA_PHY_CONFIG=0x0e262709` of the godnet/godarm SoCs). The Hi3520D vendor kernel configs (`hi3520d_full_defconfig`, `hi3520d_mini_defconfig`) use `CONFIG_HI_SATA_PHY_CONFIG=0x0e276716` (1.5G) and `CONFIG_HI_SATA_3G_PHY_CONFIG=0x0e676706` (3G); the driver writes the 3G value instead when the module parameter `mode_3g` is set. Differences from the reset value 0x0E636159: DS 1.5G 0x0E262709: gen2_en 0x1 -> 0x0, rx_dpll_mode 0x1 -> 0x3, rx_eq_val 0x5 -> 0x0, tx_edgerate 0x0 -> 0x1, tx_cko_en 0x0 -> 0x1, tx_atten 0x5 -> 0x0; vendor Hi3520D 1.5G 0x0E276716: gen2_en 0x1 -> 0x0, rx_dpll_mode 0x1 -> 0x3, tx_edgerate 0x0 -> 0x1, tx_cko_en 0x0 -> 0x1, tx_atten 0x5 -> 0x1, tx_boost 0x9 -> 0x6; vendor Hi3520D 3G 0x0E676706: rx_dpll_mode 0x1 -> 0x3, tx_edgerate 0x0 -> 0x1, tx_cko_en 0x0 -> 0x1, tx_atten 0x5 -> 0x0, tx_boost 0x9 -> 0x6.

Data sheet 14.7.7 SATA_PORT_PHYCTL (offset 0x74 + n x 0x80, printed page 14-132, `datasheet.txt` line 59137).";

